course: dictionary
lesson: 1360
title: Canine: dogs and teeth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Canine is an adjective and a noun. As an adjective, it means to do with dogs or the dog family, like wolves and foxes. As a noun, a canine is a dog or a member of the dog family.
explain: Canine also names a tooth. A canine tooth is one of the four pointed teeth next to your front teeth. Meat-eaters have big canines for tearing food. «A dog has 42 teeth and a cat has 30, and their long pointed canines make deep narrow holes» shows how they work.
explain: Context helps here. In the sentence about rodents, «no long pointed canines at all» tells you that canines are long, pointed teeth, and that rodents do not have them. Use the clues around the word to check your meaning.
fact: Canine means to do with dogs or the dog family.
fact: A canine is a dog, or a member of the dog family such as a wolf, fox or coyote.
fact: A canine tooth is one of four pointed teeth next to your front teeth, used for tearing food.
fact: «Mandrills have very long canine teeth, and a wide yawn shows them off as a warning to rivals.»
fact: Police dogs work in the «K-9» unit, which sounds like canine, so it is also called a canine unit.
exercise: Which of these is a canine? | A mouse | A squirrel | A hamster | *A fox
exercise: «Mandrills have very long canine teeth.» What is a canine tooth? | A front tooth for cutting | *A long pointed tooth next to the front teeth, used for tearing | A tooth that is only in babies | A flat tooth at the back for grinding
exercise: Police dogs work in the «canine unit». What does this unit work with? | Bicycles | *Police dogs | Cars and vans | Boats on the river
test: «What makes a rodent is its teeth... and no long pointed canines at all.» What does this tell you about rodents? | *Rodents have no long pointed canine teeth | Rodents have only canine teeth | Rodents have no canine teeth | Rodents have canines at the back
test: «Their long pointed canines make deep narrow holes that trap germs.» Why can a bite from a dog be harmful? | Canines wear away the germs | The teeth are flat and wide | *The deep narrow holes can trap germs and get infected | Dogs bite only soft food
exam: Which sentence best describes canine? | Canine means a flat tooth used for grinding food | *Canine means to do with dogs or the dog family | Canine means a small rodent with growing front teeth | Canine means a large cat with sabre teeth
